{"name":"Rubber Ducky","hex":"#facf58","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rubber ducky","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rubber duck.","A small, flexible fixed-length antenna covered with a vinyl or rubber coating, frequently used with a handy talkie or other portable radio equipment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rubber_ducky"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rubber duck","blocks":[{"text":"A rubber duck, or rubber duckie, is a toy shaped like a duck that is usually yellow with a flat base. It may be made of rubber or rubber-like material such as vinyl plastic. Rubber ducks were invented in the late 19th century when it became possible to more easily shape rubber, and are believed to improve developmental skills in children during water play."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Rubber_duckies_So_many_ducks.jpg/330px-Rubber_duckies_So_many_ducks.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rubber_duck"},{"title":"Natural rubber","blocks":[{"text":"Rubber, also called India rubber, latex, Amazonian rubber, caucho, or caoutchouc, as initially produced, consists of polymers of the organic compound isoprene, with minor impurities of other organic compounds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Caoutchouc_naturel.jpg/330px-Caoutchouc_naturel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natural_rubber"},{"title":"Ducky","blocks":[{"text":"Ducky is a nickname and fictional character given name. It may refer to:"}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ducky"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Archie_McPhee_duckies_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Archie_McPhee_duckies_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/comm